AIM :

To develop a basic Spring MVC application using annotation-based configuration, create a controller to handle user requests, and display employee details using MVC architecture without XML configuration.

PROCEDURE :
Create a Spring Boot project in Eclipse
Add dependency: Spring Web (Spring MVC)
Create a main class with @SpringBootApplication
Create an Employee model class
Create a Controller class using @Controller
Use @GetMapping to handle requests
Return employee details using MVC flow
Run the application and test in browser

Code:

package com.example.mvc;

import org.springframework.boot.SpringApplication;
import org.springframework.boot.autoconfigure.SpringBootApplication;
import org.springframework.stereotype.Controller;
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.GetMapping;
import org.springframework.ui.Model;

// -------------------- MAIN --------------------
@SpringBootApplication
public class MvcApplication {

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        SpringApplication.run(MvcApplication.class, args);
    }
}

// -------------------- MODEL --------------------
class Employee {
    private int id;
    private String name;

    public Employee(int id, String name) {
        this.id = id;
        this.name = name;
    }

    public int getId() { return id; }
    public String getName() { return name; }
}

// -------------------- CONTROLLER --------------------
@Controller
class EmployeeController {

    @GetMapping("/employee")
    public String getEmployee(Model model) {

        Employee emp = new Employee(101, "Ganesh");

        model.addAttribute("emp", emp);

        return "view"; // view name
    }
}

RESULT

Thus, a basic Spring MVC application was successfully developed using annotation-based configuration without XML. The controller handled user requests and displayed employee details through the MVC flow.
